 "narrative": "All newly delivered estimates are already signed to their registered hypothesis direction, so positive signed values support the claim and negative signed values oppose it. H85 is now independently validated and accepted: PTEN-loss cells have stronger dependency_STAT3 than PTEN-intact cells. Discovery signed estimate was +0.267 (95% CI +0.215 to +0.319, R73), and independent validation was +0.274 (independent adjusted CI +0.200 to +0.348, R79). The raw contrast is approximately -0.27, meaning a substantially more negative STAT3 dependency score in PTEN-loss cells. This is roughly one dependency-score standard deviation and is far larger than the small null effects seen across pathway modifier probes. I therefore close the main PTEN/STAT3 investigation as a robust dataset association, not as a causal or generalized biological claim. I register direct PTEN-loss contrasts within TP53-intact and TP53-loss strata to test whether the association is stable across this major co-mutational context; PIK3CA-mutation modification remains covered by the registered interaction claim H89.\n\nH64 is reassessed for its validation response deadline. Within the KY library context, TP53-intact cells had stronger dependency_USP7 than TP53-loss cells. Discovery signed estimate was +0.212 (95% CI +0.051 to +0.373, R43), and independent validation was larger, +0.336 (independent adjusted CI +0.129 to +0.544, R53). The validation interval excludes zero at the adjusted level and the magnitude is scientifically meaningful. I accept and close H64 as validated KY-library context evidence for the broader TP53-intact/USP7 association. The main TP53-intact/USP7 claim had already been independently validated, so this closes the specific context investigation.\n\nH67 remains unsupported after validation. EGFR amplification was not associated with meaningful dependency_TMED10 differences. Discovery signed estimate was +0.004 (95% CI -0.027 to +0.034, R46), and independent validation was +0.013 (independent adjusted CI -0.031 to +0.058, R80). Both intervals cross zero and the point estimates are small relative to the TMED10 score distribution. I keep H67 rejected and closed.\n\nWith these results, the dataset-supported robust associations are now: MSI-high is associated with much stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; TP53-intact status is associated with stronger USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker/less-negative NFE2L2 dependency relative to KEAP1-intact cells; and PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency. Prior accepted context results for lineage subtype, screen batch, library, and ARID1A-stratified SMARCA4/SMARCA2 remain concordant with their main effects. I close the main investigations and accepted context investigations for H9, H13, H39, H45-H51 because the main effects are validated and these direct strata were precise and concordant, while keeping unresolved context checks such as H87-H89 and the newly registered TP53-stratum PTEN checks active for further characterization. The next analyses should prioritize PTEN/STAT3 stability by TP53 and PIK3CA status, the still-untested ARID1A-loss main contrast H61, and remaining active unresolved predictors, while preserving validation capacity for any new large robust discovery rather than spending it on imprecise small-effect modifiers.",
 "research_notes": "Current robust dataset associations: (1) MSI-high -> much stronger dependency_WRN; (2) SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger dependency_SMARCA2; (3) TP53-intact -> stronger dependency_USP7; (4) KEAP1 loss -> weaker/less-negative dependency_NFE2L2; (5) PTEN loss -> stronger dependency_STAT3. PTEN/STAT3 validated: H85 discovery signed +0.267 (CI +0.215 to +0.319) and validation +0.274 (adjusted CI +0.200 to +0.348), accepted/closed. KY-library TP53/USP7 H64 validated and closed. EGFR amplification/TMED10 H67 remains null with independent CI crossing zero. Many pathway modifiers are unsupported or underpowered: NF1/ERBB2/PTEN vs EGFR, RB1 vs KIF18A/WRN, MYC vs KIF18A/POLR2A/DHX9, small KRAS/BRAF/RIT1 effects, and constructed marker controls. Accepted main and accepted strata investigations for validated associations have been closed where further testing is unnecessary. Active priorities: direct PTEN/STAT3 contrasts in TP53-intact and TP53-loss cells, H87-H89 PTEN/STAT3 lineage/PIK3CA context checks, H61 ARID1A-loss main SMARCA2 contrast, and other active unresolved predictors. Do not request validation for small CI-crossing interactions or redundant technical/context checks unless a new large robust effect emerges. All claims remain dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
